# PART 1: PROJECT VISION & OBJECTIVES

I want to build a complete Grocery E-commerce and Business Management System for my local business in Bangladesh.

This is not just an ordinary online grocery store. It must be a complete business ecosystem that allows me to manage the entire business from a centralized system.

My business model:

1. Purchase fresh vegetables and fruits directly from farmers and local markets.
2. Purchase grocery and household products from dealers, distributors and suppliers.
3. Receive purchased products at my warehouse.
4. Inspect, sort, weigh and package products.
5. Calculate actual purchase costs, transportation costs, packaging costs and other expenses.
6. Set selling prices, discounts and profit margins.
7. Publish products on the customer-facing e-commerce website.
8. Receive orders online and through delivery representatives.
9. Manage order processing, inventory and delivery operations.
10. Collect customer payments through Cash on Delivery.
11. Manage delivery staff, managers, employees and accountants.
12. Maintain complete financial records.
13. Manage investor loans, profit-sharing investments and withdrawals.
14. Visualize business performance through professional dashboards and reports.

Initially, the business will operate in one Upazila in Bangladesh.

However, the system architecture must support future expansion to multiple Upazilas, warehouses, outlets and business locations without requiring a complete system redesign.

The entire application must be developed using Core PHP / Raw PHP without Laravel or any other PHP framework.

The code must be clean, understandable, modular, maintainable and suitable for real commercial operations.

