# PART 29: BUSINESS RULES THAT MUST NEVER BE VIOLATED

1. Cart operations must not reduce physical stock.
2. Stock reservation and stock deduction must be separate.
3. Every stock change must create a movement record.
4. Every purchase must retain supplier and batch information.
5. Historical order costs must never be silently recalculated.
6. Delivery status and payment status must be separate.
7. Delivered does not automatically mean paid.
8. Cash collection must be verified.
9. Cash handover must have sender and receiver confirmation.
10. A delivery man's direct order must retain that delivery man's ID.
11. A cancelled order must not generate normal delivery commission.
12. Returned products must undergo inspection before restocking.
13. Expired products must not be sold.
14. Sorting loss must not be treated as a sale.
15. Investor loan principal must not be treated as ordinary expenses.
16. Loan repayments must not be confused with profit distributions.
17. Profit-sharing capital must be separate from loan liabilities.
18. Unrealized inventory profit must not be included in realized profit.
19. Financial transactions must be auditable.
20. Financial corrections must use reversal entries.
21. Multiple warehouses must maintain separate stock.
22. Stock transfers must not create or destroy inventory.
23. All important operations must be permission-controlled.
24. Reports must reconcile with their source transactions.

